  },
  "articleBody": "Living in a log home is amazing, but keeping it protected from Colorado’s diverse weather can be a bit of a challenge. The sun, wind, rain, and snow are constantly trying to break down those beautiful logs. Don't worry though, there are definitely things you can do to keep your home looking its best and prevent costly damage. Proactive protection is always better than reacting to problems! Firstly, make sure your roof overhangs are doing their job. Longer overhangs protect your logs from direct sun and heavy rain, especially on south-facing walls. Secondly, keep your gutters clean and in good repair. Clogged gutters can cause water to spill over and saturate your logs, leading to rot. Thirdly, maintain a good distance between your logs and the ground. Landscaping, decks, and even splash-back from rain can contribute to moisture problems. Try to keep vegetation trimmed away from the walls to allow for air circulation. Lastly, and perhaps most importantly, regularly inspect and maintain your log finish. High-quality stains and sealants are your log home's first line of defense against the elements. If you notice fading, peeling, or cracking, it’s a sign that your finish is failing and needs attention. HH Remodeling LLC offers refinishing log and cabin services, so we're experienced in what it takes to protect your home. We can help assess your log home’s condition and recommend the right solutions to keep it robust and beautiful for years to come. Let us help you make your house feel more like a home, safe from the weather’s whims.",
